cerbation reduce likelihood"], "alarm_features": ["Syncope", "Uncharacterised ECG Abnormality"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Acute Myocardial Injury / Infarction", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.022262566662884377, "posterior": 0.010247948663854707, "danger": 0.95, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The positional relief when leaning forward is a classic sign of pericarditis, providing moderate support for B2 and mild against B1. Structural cardiac disease (B3) is unrelated to this finding, remaining neutral.", "No evidence of diffuse ST elevation was found to strongly confirm pericarditis (B2), but the absence weakens B1 (MI) due to atypical pattern. This results in moderate against for B1, but insufficient to upgrade B2's probability."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is there ST-segment elevation in the ECG?", "Are there symptoms of left ventricular failure?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Cardiac troponin levels", "ECG ST/T wave analysis"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 3, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 1.0, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Acute Pericardial Inflammation with Chest Pain", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.5522750482242142, "posterior": 0.5969210048717924, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The positional relief when leaning forward is a classic sign of pericarditis, providing moderate support for B2 and mild against B1. Structural cardiac disease (B3) is unrelated to this finding, remaining neutral."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3", "B2.4"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Does the pain change with chest position?", "Is there pericardial friction rub on exam?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["ECG for diffuse ST elevation", "Pericardial effusion ultrasound"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.85, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "urGENCY"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Structural Cardiac Disease with Exertional Symptom Exacerbation", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.02682489629802459, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Positional relief and syncope moderately align with viral pericarditis as mechanical/compressive effects are plausible."]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Electrolyte Disturbance with Cardiac Consequences", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.005588520062088456, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["No ECG findings were identified to support electrolyte disturbances. This neutralizes B4 (hyperkalemia/hypokalemia) while structural cardiac disease (B3) remains unaffected."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Non-cardiac Causes of Acute Chest Pain and Syncope", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.006706224074506147, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (STEMI)", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0017603838195578638, "danger": 0.98, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Absence of ST elevation is expected in non-STEMI etiologies and reduces STEMI probability."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Non-ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (NSTEMI) or Unstable Angina", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.011233405196868261, "posterior": 0.003457896788417232, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Troponin trends strongly support NSTEMI/unstable angina, but current absence of data keeps this speculative.", "No viral history slightly weakens viral pericarditis, but lack of ST elevation keeps it as the leading pericarditis subtype."], "evidence_against": ["Absence of diffuse ST elevation argues moderately against non-STE MI/unstable angina due to atypical pain pattern.", "Positional relief and absence of infection signs strongly argue against non-STE MI, favoring pericardial diagnosis."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Are there symptoms of acute coronary syndrome like transient CP or prior MI history?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["High-sensitivity troponin trend (serial measurements)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Acute Myocardial Injury without Infarction (e.g., Takotsubo Cardiomyopathy)", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.005029668055879611, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Acute Viral Pericarditis", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.5293997503687735, "posterior": 0.586660482037798, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Positional relief and syncope moderately align with viral pericarditis as mechanical/compressive effects are plausible.", "Positional relief and absence of infection signs strongly argue against non-STE MI, favoring pericardial diagnosis."], "evidence_against": ["No viral history slightly weakens viral pericarditis, but lack of ST elevation keeps it as the leading pericarditis subtype."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["History of recent viral upper respiratory infection?", "Does the chest pain improve with NSAIDs like ibuprofen?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Inflammatory markers (CRP, ESR) for acute inflammation confirmation", "Viral pericarditis serology (e.g., Coxsackie antibodies)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2.2": {"id": "B2.2", "label": "Bacterial (Purulent) Pericarditis", "level": 2, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.003017800833527766, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Normotension and absence of fever decisively reduce bacterial pericarditis likelihood, moderately supporting viral pericarditis."]}, "B2.3": {"id": "B2.3", "label": "Idiopathic or Recurrent Pericarditis", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.004023734444703687, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "B2", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B2.4": {"id": "B2.4", "label": "Neoplastic or Autoimmune Pericarditis", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.006535799387268806, "posterior": 0.00321898755576295, "danger": 0.55, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Diabetes does not appreciably increase neoplastic pericarditis likelihood; no contradiction to viral pericarditis assumption."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Signs of systemic disease (e.g., rash, arthritis) in history?", "Known malignancy in medical history?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Autoimmune panel (ANA, rheumatoid factor),", "Pericardial fluid cytology for atypical cells"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 3, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.55, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}}, "frontier": ["B2.1", "B2.1", "B1.2", "B2.4"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the positional relief with leaning forward (E3) and lack of systemic infection signs (E7) strongly rule out non-STE MI/unstable angina as a high-danger diagnosis?", "result_summary": "Positional relief and absence of infection signs strongly argue against non-STE MI, favoring pericardial diagnosis.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "strong_against", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "strong_against", "B2": "strong_for", "B2.1": "moderate_for", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 4, "bundle_id": 4, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Would the patient's diabetes/malignancy risk profile (E5) increase the likelihood of neoplastic over viral pericarditis, contradicting B2.1's assumed etiology?", "result_summary": "Diabetes does not appreciably increase neoplastic pericarditis likelihood; no contradiction to viral pericarditis assumption.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1": "neutral", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B2.1": "neutral", "B2.4": "weak_against", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 5, "bundle_id": 5, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do positional relief of pain when leaning forward (E3) and syncope (E4) provide moderate support for viral pericarditis (B2.1) despite lack of direct evidence for viral etiology?", "result_summary": ""}, {"timestep": 5, "bundle_id": 5, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's transient syncope (E4) with positional improvement (E3) create a unique scenario where NSTEMI/unstable angina (B1.2) still remains clinically plausible?", "result_summary": ""}, {"timestep": 5, "bundle_id": 5, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Would the absence of documented viral upper respiratory infection (not in evidence) diminish confidence in viral pericarditis (B2.1) in the absence of alternative explanations?", "result_summary": ""}, {"timestep": 5, "bundle_id": 5, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the absence of diffuse ST elevation in ECG (E9) with positional variation (E3) constitute definitive evidence against NSTEMI/unstable angina as a high-danger diagnosis?", "result_summary": ""}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.0638957015618949, "B2": 0.4507551310184587, "B3": 0.06195946818123143, "B4": 0.012908222537756548, "B5": 0.015489867045307857, "B1.1": 0.02033045049696656, "B1.2": 0.03194785078094745, "B1.3": 0.011617400283980894, "B2.1": 0.4182264102233122, "B2.2": 0.01394088034077707, "B2.3": 0.009293920227184713, "B2.4": 0.009293920227184713}, {"B1": 0.022262566662884377, "B2": 0.5522750482242142, "B3": 0.04357199591512538, "B4": 0.009077499148984454, "B5": 0.010892998978781345, "B1.1": 0.002859412231930103, "B1.2": 0.011233405196868261, "B1.3": 0.00816974923408601, "B2.1": 0.5293997503687735, "B2.2": 0.00980369908090321, "B2.3": 0.006535799387268806, "B2.4": 0.006535799387268806}, {"B1": 0.010247948663854707, "B2": 0.5969210048717924, "B3": 0.02682489629802459, "B4": 0.005588520062088456, "B5": 0.006706224074506147, "B1.1": 0.0017603838195578638, "B1.2": 0.003457896788417232, "B1.3": 0.005029668055879611, "B2.1": 0.586660482037798, "B2.2": 0.003017800833527766, "B2.3": 0.004023734444703687, "B2.4": 0.00321898755576295}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No urgent instability markers currently present, and leading differentials (pericarditis) are not time-critical. Syncope resolved with no ongoing neurological deficits, vitals stable without shock, and absence of airway/respiratory compromise.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch B2.1's posterior (0.5866) remains below the 0.75 threshold for confirmation. B1 (MI) has dangerously high 0.95 but posterior (0.0102) <0.10. Unresolved discriminators like viral URTI history (askable) and troponin (requestable) remain available for refinement."}, "turn_budget_used": 4, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.42, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.586660482037798, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_vignette": "A 50-year-old man presents to the emergency department with chest pain. He states that the pain is dull in quality, started 30 minutes ago, has been gradually worsening, and is worse with exertion. He also endorses some shortness of breath. He also believes the pain is worse when leaning back and improved when leaning forward. His wife noticed he fainted after the pain started but regained consciousness shortly after. He has a medical history of diabetes and hypertension for which he is on metformin and losartan. His temperature is 99.2°F (37.3°C), blood pressure is 130/87 mmHg, pulse is 99/min, respirations are 22/min, and oxygen saturation is 100% on room air. Physical exam reveals an overweight man. A normal S1 and S2 are auscultated with clear breath sounds. An ECG is performed as seen in Figure A.", "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Hyperkalemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Hypertrophic obstructive cardiomyopathy"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Hypokalemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Myocardial infarction"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Pericarditis"}], "static_evidence_items": [{"id": "E1", "kind": "direct", "content": "Chief complaint: chest pain", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E2", "kind": "direct", "content": "Pain characteristics: dull, onset 30 minutes ago, gradually worsening with exertion", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E3", "kind": "direct", "content": "Pain relieved by leaning forward and worsened by leaning back", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E4", "kind": "direct", "content": "Syncope reported by wife shortly after pain onset, with spontaneous return to consciousness", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E5", "kind": "direct", "content": "Medical history: diabetes mellitus and hypertension", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E6", "kind": "direct", "content": "Current medications: metformin and losartan", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E7", "kind": "direct", "content": "Vital signs: temperature 99.2°F (37.3°C), blood pressure 130/87 mmHg, pulse 99/min, respirations 22/min, oxygen saturation 100% on room air", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E8", "kind": "direct", "content": "Physical findings: overweight patient, with normal S1/S2 heart sounds and clear breath sounds", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}, {"id": "E9", "kind": "image_reference", "content": "ECG is performed as seen in Figure A — image not available in text form", "source_ids": [], "independent": true, "branch_links": {}, "metadata": {}}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Exertional Chest Pain', 'Pericarditis', 'Constrictive pericarditis', 'Chest discomfort', 'Myocardial infarction'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3}, "raw_result": [{"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do positional relief of pain when leaning forward (E3) and syncope (E4) provide moderate support for viral pericarditis (B2.1) despite lack of direct evidence for viral etiology?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Do positional relief of pain when leaning forward (E3) and syncope (E4) provide moderate support for viral pericarditis (B2.1) despite lack of direct evidence for viral etiology?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient's transient syncope (E4) with positional improvement (E3) create a unique scenario where NSTEMI/unstable angina (B1.2) still remains clinically plausible?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Does the patient's transient syncope (E4) with positional improvement (E3) create a unique scenario where NSTEMI/unstable angina (B1.2) still remains clinically plausible?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Would the absence of documented viral upper respiratory infection (not in evidence) diminish confidence in viral pericarditis (B2.1) in the absence of alternative explanations?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Would the absence of documented viral upper respiratory infection (not in evidence) diminish confidence in viral pericarditis (B2.1) in the absence of alternative explanations?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}, {"action": {"type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the absence of diffuse ST elevation in ECG (E9) with positional variation (E3) constitute definitive evidence against NSTEMI/unstable angina as a high-danger diagnosis?"}, "raw_result": {"analysis_target": "Could the absence of diffuse ST elevation in ECG (E9) with positional variation (E3) constitute definitive evidence against NSTEMI/unstable angina as a high-danger diagnosis?", "evidence_items_ref": "see state.static_evidence_items", "question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?"}}], "lr_reference": "[LR Reference for 'Chest pain' (source: BODHI-S, Guideline_common)]\n  Structural Cardiac Disease with Exertional Symptom Exacerbation: no data\n  Non-ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (NSTEMI) or Unstable Angina: qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Acute Myocardial Injury without Infarction (e.g., Takotsubo Cardiomyopathy): qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Acute Viral Pericarditis: qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Idiopathic or Recurrent Pericarditis: qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Neoplastic or Autoimmune Pericarditis: LR+=0.9236, LR-=1.0466 (Sn=0.35, Sp=0.6211, confidence=low) [EBM: minimal decrease → suggests neutral/weak_against]\n[LR Reference for 'Dull pain' (source: Guideline_common, subsumption_upward:docLogica)]\n  Structural Cardiac Disease with Exertional Symptom Exacerbation: no data\n  Non-ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (NSTEMI) or Unstable Angina: LR+≈1.5518 (subsumption: 'dull pain' IS-A 'myocardial rupture (free wall)', depth=3, attenuation=0.3999999999999999) [EBM: minimal increase → suggests neutral/weak_for]\n  Acute Myocardial Injury without Infarction (e.g., Takotsubo Cardiomyopathy): no data\n  Acute Viral Pericarditis: qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Idiopathic or Recurrent Pericarditis: qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Neoplastic or Autoimmune Pericarditis: qualitative association (no LR available)\n[LR Reference for 'moderate to severe back pain that is worse with movement' (source: Guideline_common, PrimeKG-2hop)]\n  Structural Cardiac Disease with Exertional Symptom Exacerbation: no data\n  Non-ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (NSTEMI) or Unstable Angina: qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Acute Myocardial Injury without Infarction (e.g., Takotsubo Cardiomyopathy): qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Acute Viral Pericarditis: indirect chain LR+≈5.581 (path: moderate to severe back pain that is worse with movement → arthralgia → Acute Viral Pericarditis, confidence=indirect_chain) [EBM: moderate increase → suggests moderate_for]\n  Idiopathic or Recurrent Pericarditis: no data\n  Neoplastic or Autoimmune Pericarditis: no data\n[LR Reference for 'Inertia' (source: subsumption_upward:docLogica)]\n  Structural Cardiac Disease with Exertional Symptom Exacerbation: no data\n  Non-ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (NSTEMI) or Unstable Angina: LR+≈1.3904 (subsumption: 'inertia' IS-A 'myocardial rupture (free wall)', depth=8, attenuation=0.3) [EBM: minimal increase → suggests neutral/weak_for]\n  Acute Myocardial Injury without Infarction (e.g., Takotsubo Cardiomyopathy): no data\n  Acute Viral Pericarditis: no data\n  Idiopathic or Recurrent Pericarditis: no data\n  Neoplastic or Autoimmune Pericarditis: no data\n[LR Reference for 'Increased carrying angle' (source: subsumption_upward:docLogica)]\n  Structural Cardiac Disease with Exertional Symptom Exacerbation: no data\n  Non-ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (NSTEMI) or Unstable Angina: LR+≈1.3904 (subsumption: 'increased carrying angle' IS-A 'myocardial rupture (free wall)', depth=7, attenuation=0.3) [EBM: minimal increase → suggests neutral/weak_for]\n  Acute Myocardial Injury without Infarction (e.g., Takotsubo Cardiomyopathy): no data\n  Acute Viral Pericarditis: no data\n  Idiopathic or Recurrent Pericarditis: no data\n  Neoplastic or Autoimmune Pericarditis: no data\n[LR Reference for 'Loss of consciousness' (source: Guideline_common)]\n  Structural Cardiac Disease with Exertional Symptom Exacerbation: no data\n  Non-ST-Elevation Myocardial Infarction (NSTEMI) or Unstable Angina: qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Acute Myocardial Injury without Infarction (e.g., Takotsubo Cardiomyopathy): qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Acute Viral Pericarditis: no data\n  Idiopathic or Recurrent Pericarditis: qualitative association (no LR available)\n  Neoplastic or Autoimmune Pericarditis: no data\n[LR Reference for 'Hypertension' (source: subsumption_upward:docLogica)]\n  Structura"}
